# save: 09-MondoMole
# Sweep segment 09 -> 10: the Happy Happy drug store phone out to Lilliput Steps (Happy Happy's
# east cave: the spiral walk, Auto Fight battles, overworld Lifeup alpha), Mondo Mole (manual:
# Paula PSI Shield alpha, then Ness and Paula bash while the mole's PSI shield is up; a first
# take lost at L23/L16 and was cut), the Lilliput Steps melody, back down the spiral, Happy
# Happy, the valley cave, Peaceful Rest Valley reversed (switchback, log bridge, west bank), the
# Twoson cave rooms, Twoson, Polestar Preschool (Paula's father: FLG_POLA), the phone call,
# Burglin Park, Everdred (Wad of bills; leaving his house the party bounces through the door
# pair 5 times, in both games), the Runaway Five member (Backstage pass), the photographer,
# the Chaos Theater (pass on the ticket man, backstage, the show), the manager (Wad of bills;
# "Oh, pardon me" moves the ticket man out of the counter gap first), the Twoson hotel phone:
# Dad, Record, Continue (10-ToThreed starts there). Recorded in chunks with playtest/sweep/rec.py
# late-pads: the port replays the pads the original read after each lag-merged frame
# Doors: skip K / lag / ignore: idle K+30; other idle masks are post-battle fade-ins. `# lag:`
# numbers are emu logic frames: K+20 lands that many frames early once lag lines pile up, and
# the later ones are placed with the emu frame of port frame K+20 instead.
# The preschool, Everdred's house, the theater lobby (both ways) and the backstage TELEPORT_TO
# loads spend more CPU-time frames in the original (the emu's LSTEP jumps 3 during the load),
# so their pairs carry 3 / 2 / 3 / 7 lag lines; idle 57272-57275 is that lobby fade's end.
# party 25323-25560: Ness's HP meter rolls up from the sanctuary heal through the first battle
# after it; the original's roller phase (FRAME_COUNTER & 3) shifts at the battle-entry lag
# (docs/known-original-behaviour.md, rolling meter row), 1 HP apart for ~190 frames
# late-pads
